# Cache Handling

`@furystack/cache` provides a Cache with built-in Observable integration. App code consumes data via services that own caches; components subscribe via `getObservable`. See `FRONTEND_PATTERNS.mdc` for the service-cache contract.

## Basic setup

The `Impl` class + `defineService` token pattern is the canonical pi-rat shape — see `CODE_STYLE.mdc` § "DI — functional services" and `FRONTEND_PATTERNS.mdc` for the full service/cache wiring. Here only the cache-specific bits:

```typescript
import { Cache } from '@furystack/cache'
import { defineService, type Token } from '@furystack/inject'

class UsersServiceImpl implements Disposable {
  public userCache = new Cache({
    capacity: 100,
    load: async (id: string) => {
      const { result } = await this.apiClient.call({
        method: 'GET',
        action: '/users/:id',
        url: { id },
        query: {},
      })
      return result
    },
  })

  constructor(private readonly apiClient: IdentityApiClient) {}

  public getUser = this.userCache.get.bind(this.userCache)
  public getUserAsObservable = this.userCache.getObservable.bind(this.userCache)

  public [Symbol.dispose](): void {
    this.userCache[Symbol.dispose]()
  }
}

export type UsersService = UsersServiceImpl
export const UsersService: Token<UsersService, 'singleton'> = defineService({ /* ... */ })
```

## Individual + query cache pattern

For list endpoints, run two caches: one keyed by `id`, one keyed by `FindOptions`. Populate the individual cache from list results so detail pages don't refetch.

```typescript
public seriesCache = new Cache({
  capacity: 100,
  load: async (id: string) => { /* GET /series/:id */ },
})

public seriesQueryCache = new Cache({
  capacity: 100,
  load: async (findOptions: FindOptions<Series, Array<keyof Series>>) => {
    const { result } = await this.mediaApiClient.call({ method: 'GET', action: '/series', query: { findOptions } })
    result.entries.forEach((entry) => {
      this.seriesCache.setExplicitValue({
        loadArgs: [entry.imdbId],
        value: { status: 'loaded', value: entry, updatedAt: new Date() },
      })
    })
    return result
  },
})
```

## Methods

| Method | Use |
|---|---|
| `get(...args)` | async fetch, cache miss runs `load` |
| `getObservable(...args)` | reactive subscription for components — emits `loading` / `loaded` / `error` cache states |
| `setExplicitValue({ loadArgs, value })` | manually populate a cache entry (e.g. after a mutation, or from a list query) |
| `reload(...args)` | force refetch (await it in service methods, see TESTING_GUIDELINES) |
| `flushAll()` | invalidate all entries (typical for query caches after mutations) |
| `remove(...args)` | drop a single entry |

## Component subscription

```typescript
const MovieDetails = Shade<{ movieId: string }>({
  customElementName: 'movie-details',
  render: ({ props, injector, useObservable }) => {
    const movieService = injector.get(MovieService)
    const [state] = useObservable('movie', movieService.movieCache.getObservable(props.movieId))

    if (!state || state.status === 'loading') return <div>Loading...</div>
    if (state.status === 'failed') return (
      <div style={{ color: 'red' }}>
        Failed to load.
        <button onclick={() => void movieService.movieCache.reload(props.movieId)}>Retry</button>
      </div>
    )
    if (state.status === 'loaded') return <h1>{state.value.title}</h1>
    return null
  },
})
```

Always handle all three cache states. The full union from `getObservable` is `loading | loaded | obsolete | failed` (depending on cache version) — check `state.status` before reading `state.value`.

## Invalidation after mutations

```typescript
public updateUser = async (username: string, body: UserUpdate) => {
  const { result } = await this.apiClient.call({ method: 'PATCH', action: '/users/:id', url: { id: username }, body })
  await this.userCache.reload(username)   // refresh detail cache
  this.userQueryCache.flushAll()          // drop list caches
  return result
}
```

Always `await` the reload — fire-and-forget triggers unhandled rejections in tests after the injector disposes (see `TESTING_GUIDELINES.mdc`).

## Capacity guidance

| Data shape | Capacity |
|---|---|
| Frequently changing recent items | 20 |
| Frequent + balanced (entities, movies) | 100 |
| Stable per-user data (preferences) | 500+ |

## Error handling in `load`

Errors thrown from `load` set the cache entry to `failed` — components reading via `getObservable` see `state.status === 'failed'`. Log with context before re-throwing or wrapping.

```typescript
public seriesCache = new Cache({
  capacity: 100,
  load: async (id: string) => {
    try {
      const { result } = await this.mediaApiClient.call({ method: 'GET', action: '/series/:id', url: { id }, query: {} })
      return result
    } catch (error) {
      await this.logger.error({ message: 'Failed to load series', data: { seriesId: id, error } })
      throw error
    }
  },
})
```

## Type safety

Use explicit generics for the cache type:

```typescript
public seriesCache: Cache<[string], Series> = new Cache({ /* ... */ })
public seriesQueryCache: Cache<[FindOptions<Series, Array<keyof Series>>], SeriesQueryResult> = new Cache({ /* ... */ })
```
